# One RAM session on polaris: bring the CPU up, prove the clock, then stop.
#
# Deliberately short. raphael's list runs a GPU render and a touch session because that board
# has been brought that far; polaris has not, so this asks only the questions whose answers
# are already known to work on this kernel, and adds nothing that would need a driver that
# does not exist yet. Each line's output is evidence for exactly one claim:
#
#   cpu_test        - the four A55s come up and run in parallel
#   rwtouch wait    - the input device opens and waits (it will time out with touchscreen=0,
#                     which is the correct result until raphael_touch.c has a polaris path)
#   ps -A           - what actually got launched, so a missing binary is visible rather than
#                     inferred from silence
#
# Not here on purpose: gl_test (no A630 path in hakios.adreno.c yet), net_test (no WCN3990
# bring-up), camera, haptics. Adding them now would only produce timeouts that look like
# failures of the kernel instead of failures of work not yet done.
/redwood/bin/hello_dyn polaris combined hardware test
/redwood/bin/cpu_test
/redwood/bin/cpu_test 45 &
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 20
/bin/ps -A
